course: dictionary
lesson: 6038
title: Meltwater and the world of ice
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Meltwater is water that comes from melting snow or ice. You can work it out from the two parts: melt, which means turning from solid into liquid, and water. When snow and ice warm up, the water they leave behind is meltwater.
explain: Read the context. «Adelie and gentoo penguins build nests of pebbles that keep eggs out of meltwater and mud.» The eggs need to stay away from the water, so meltwater must be water that can spread and cause trouble. Try your meaning in the sentence: "keep eggs out of water from melting ice and mud" still makes sense, so you have the right idea.
explain: Meltwater often appears with places and changes of season, such as «spring meltwater», «glacial meltwater», «meltwater streams» and «meltwater lake». When you see these phrases in geography or science, think of rivers, glaciers and ice melting.
fact: Meltwater is water from melting snow or ice, especially from glaciers and ice sheets.
fact: In spring, meltwater feeds rivers.
fact: Meltwater can carve valleys and form lakes at the edges of glaciers.
fact: Meltwater can cause sudden floods, so it can be dangerous.
fact: Meltwater is uncountable: you say «some meltwater», not «meltwaters».
exercise: «Adelie and gentoo penguins build nests of pebbles that keep eggs out of meltwater and mud.» What is meltwater here? | Mud from the river bank | Rain that falls in summer | Salty water from the sea | *Water from melting snow or ice
exercise: Which word could replace meltwater in «Spring ___ fills the river»? | Pebble | Penguin | *Meltwater | Sunshine
exercise: Why can meltwater be dangerous? | *It can cause sudden floods | It stops penguins from swimming | It turns snow into sand | It makes the sea taste sweet
test: «Adelie and gentoo penguins build nests of pebbles that keep eggs out of meltwater and mud.» Where are the eggs kept safest? | Under the river bank | In the sea | *On a pebble nest, out of the meltwater | On the bare ground in the mud
test: Meltwater is best described as: | A kind of frozen rain | *Water that comes from melting snow or ice | Dry dust from old rocks | Water that is salty like the sea
exam: Which sentence uses meltwater correctly? | The meltwater was very tall and green. | We bought three meltwaters at the shop. | Meltwaters are sold in small packets. | *The river rose quickly after the spring meltwater arrived.
